	"description": [
		"In this study of African-Americans in U. S. society from African origins to the present, students explore the African heritage, the experience of slavery, segregation, and the rise of the Civil Rights movement of the 1960s. The course pays particular attention to the issue of black nationalism as a force in American life. Offered most years. Counts towards American studies and ARMS majors and ARMS and Africa & the Americas concentrations."
